    "created_at": "2016-03-23T18:52:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-23T18:52:49Z",
    "body": "If 2 pages are subscribed to notifications, and one of them calls [`stopNotifications()`](https://webbluetoothcg.github.io/web-bluetooth/#dom-bluetoothremotegattcharacteristic-stopnotifications), that doesn't unsubscribe the other one, in the current specification. It's true that exposing CCC descriptor access would give us a uniform API to read the state, and to control whether notifications or indications get enabled, but I think we'd still want to intercept uses of that descriptor to prevent pages from interfering with each other.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
